// English: the base game's blocks, items, creatures, biomes and weather (see core/lang/en.ron
// for how language files work). Every key here is in ja.ron too, and the other way round.
// Where a definition writes its own English (a creature's or effect's title, a quest's
// why), this says the same: a test keeps them alike. A block made from a template is named
// by its member's name with the family's filled in: `block.base.{name}_log` and
// `family.base.oak` make Oak Log.
